source_event: Kannel 1.4.5 r12 byte-case mismatch, native libc diagnostics, and r18 full14/14 plus installed5/5 W3_PASS on 2026-10-13 2026-10-14 current CI repair; kannel-ci-repair-w3-20261013-r101, official CI log SHA256 e5cde636a55bc6f30b6927231665697a4cfd9d02124d68942d8750ef91d164a9; Current worker logs provide the independent second-failure boundary after the earlier checkout/fixture repair: successful source retrieval and dependency installation are not proof that configure generated usable config files. Use both-branch source reconciliation, timestamp-preserving production-helper tests and complete native recipe/tests; do not treat a missing-curl predownload warning as the cause when source() already succeeded. This extends the existing evidence/transport topic with a causal validation boundary, not a new generic umask claim. 2026-10-14 current CI repair; kannel-ci-repair-w3-20261013-r202, official CI log SHA256 65044d7f0ab4a2472c2a3cad980ae5b2ee76bfe18bfc4a0814bb80542f08481e; The current worker built the producer and initial CMake consumer successfully, then its second direct compiler invocation failed inside SDK lld only under the combined conanbuild/conanrun environment. Preserve the same source, gw-config flags and all six consumer groups; do not hard-code SDK paths, drop assertions, or modify shared dependency libraries. Compiler success without host runenv and full native consumers distinguish this package-owned scope problem from worker-wide missing SDK runtime provisioning.

